      "font_size": 19.99,
      "bold": true
    }
  },
  {
    "element_type": "paragraph",
    "text": "​Underneath the specialty workflows sits what ScImage calls the​\n​Interoperability Core, which handles:​",
    "page": 5,
    "heading_level": null,
    "heading_path": [
      "​COMPANY PROFILE​",
      "​2.7 Cross-Cutting: Interoperability​"
    ],
    "metadata": {
      "extraction_method": "pymupdf"
    }
  },
  {
    "element_type": "paragraph",
    "text": "​●​ ​HL7, EHR, DICOM, and non-DICOM data exchange​\n​●​ ​Billing and patient-ID reconciliation across systems​\n​●​ ​Connections to legacy EHRs, external reporting systems, VNAs​",
    "page": 6,
    "heading_level": null,
    "heading_path": [
      "​COMPANY PROFILE​",
      "​2.7 Cross-Cutting: Interoperability​"
    ],
    "metadata": {
      "extraction_method": "pymupdf"
    }
  },
  {
    "element_type": "paragraph",
    "text": "​(vendor-neutral archives), and third-party PACS​\n​●​ ​Support for flexible exchange patterns: subspecialty reading,​",
    "page": 6,
    "heading_level": null,
    "heading_path": [
      "​COMPANY PROFILE​",
      "​2.7 Cross-Cutting: Interoperability​"
    ],
    "metadata": {
      "extraction_method": "pymupdf"
    }
  },
  {
    "element_type": "paragraph",
    "text": "​teleradiology, consolidated worklists, and HIE/MPI (health information​\n​exchange/master patient index) translation​",
    "page": 6,
    "heading_level": null,
    "heading_path": [
      "​COMPANY PROFILE​",
      "​2.7 Cross-Cutting: Interoperability​"
    ],
    "metadata": {
      "extraction_method": "pymupdf"
    }
  },
  {
    "element_type": "paragraph",
    "text": "​This is the layer that lets a single radiology group serve multiple institutions​\n​with different EHRs, or multiple groups serve one institution, without​\n​manual reconciliation.​",
    "page": 6,
    "heading_level": null,
    "heading_path": [
